hpc:Host a owl:Class .
hpc:Officialname rdfs:domain hpc:Host .
hpc:Officialname rdfs:range xsd:string .
hpc:Alias rdfs:domain hpc:Host .
hpc:Alias rdfs:range xsd:string .
hpc:hasinterface a owl:ObjectProperty .
hpc:Hasinterface rdfs:domain hpc:Host .
hpc:Hasinterface rdfs:range hpc:Interface .

hpc:Interface a owl:Class .
hpc:Ipaddress rdfs:domain hpc:Interface .
hpc:Ipaddress rdfs:range xsd:string .


This ontology fragment defines two classes: `hpc:Host` and `hpc:Interface`. It also defines an object property `hpc:Hasinterface` that connects a host to its interfaces. Additionally, it defines datatype properties `hpc:Officialname` and `hpc:Ipaddress` for a host and an interface, respectively. The domain and range of these properties are specified using `rdfs:domain` and `rdfs:range`.
